**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `kit-acceptance`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** The library holds a pulled-source record row beside every pulled version, and the import seam answers the versions a source's records minted, which an update re-fetches (001 §C 'What it holds: … pulled-source records (§D)'; 001 §D 'A pulled record becomes a user material version in the database, with provenance'; the S13.1 brief 'a pulled-source record row (S2.1)'). The row is derived from the version's provenance, as its facet rows are derived from its envelope (step 64), so every path that stores a version keeps it: a pull, a kit snapshot's import of a version pulled elsewhere, and the re-import of an exported one. A fork (`ForkProvenance`, step 91) belongs to the user and has no row. The database model is unchanged: step 60's `LibraryPulledSourceRow` already holds the columns. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueImport.fs`, before `CatalogueImportProxy`: `PulledRecord = { version : LibraryVersionRef; pull : SourcePullInfo }` (`LibraryVersionRef`, step 137): one held version and the record it was pulled from. `CatalogueImportProxy` gains `pulledRecordsOf : MaterialSourceName -> Result<PulledRecord list, CatalogueImportError>`, with a one-line doc: every held version, whatever its lifecycle, whose provenance is `SourcePullProvenance` of that source, in ordinal order of the record's text, then of the entry's GUID text, then ascending by version. The in-memory double (`createInMemory`, step 95) answers it from its map's envelopes, and `CatalogueImportProxyTests`' `recordingProxy` (step 94) answers `Ok []`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/LibraryDatabaseStore.fs`, beside `facetRows` (step 64) and carrying step 62's `StorageBoundary` mark: `member this.pulledSourceRows : LibraryPulledSourceRow list` on `LibraryEntryEnvelope` answers, for a content under `SourcePullProvenance info`, one row with `EntryId` and `Version` from the content and `Source`, `RecordPath`, `SourceVersion`, `Licence` and `Citation` from the texts of `info`'s `source`, `record`, `sourceVersion`, `licence` and `citation` (step 60's columns), and none for any other provenance. `stageVersion` (step 67) makes the version's pulled-source rows exactly its envelope's `pulledSourceRows`, as it does its facet and sample-material rows; `stageRemoval`'s cascade already removes them (step 60). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueImportStore.fs`: `createInDatabase` (step 95) answers `pulledRecordsOf source` in one `database.run`: the `PulledSources` rows whose `Source` is the source's text (step 60's `Source`, `RecordPath` index), each version read through `tryStoredVersion` (step 67) and answered with its envelope's `SourcePullInfo`, in the order of (1); a row whose version is missing or whose provenance is not a pull is `LibraryRowInvalidErr` naming the entry and the version, and every `StorageError` is `ImportStoreUnavailableErr` with its `describe`, as its other fields answer (step 95). No cache, query option or other field is added. (4) Tests. `CatalogueImportContract` (step 95) gains `the pulled records of a source are its held pulled versions, by record, entry and version`, so it runs over `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests`: after `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries` (step 113) puts, each built with `LibraryEntryContent.ofMaterialEntry` of the catalogue's Silicon under a test-local GUID: entry A at version 1 and at version 2, both pulled from `MaterialSourceName "Test source"` record `b/x.yml`; entry B at version 1 pulled from `Test source` record `a/y.yml`; entry C at version 1 pulled from `Other source`; a fork of A's version 1 under its own GUID; and a user material. `pulledRecordsOf (MaterialSourceName "Test source")` answers exactly B v1, A v1 and A v2, in that order, each with the `SourcePullInfo` it was put with, its `recordHash` included; `Other source` answers C v1 alone; and `Unknown source` answers `[]`. `LibraryDatabaseTests` gains `a pulled version's pulled-source row is stored beside its version row, and no other version has one`: over `BuiltinCatalogue.freshLibraryDatabase ()` (step 67), `stageVersion` of a pulled envelope and of a user envelope, saved in one `run`, leaves exactly one `PulledSources` row, whose seven columns are the pulled envelope's; `stageRemoval` of that entry then leaves none.

**Acceptance.** After the rows land, every stored version under `SourcePullProvenance` MUST have its pulled-source row and no other version one, and `CatalogueImportProxy.pulledRecordsOf` MUST answer a source's pulled versions with their provenance over both stores; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the pulled records of a source are its held pulled versions, by record, entry and version` over `CatalogueImportInMemoryTests` and `CatalogueImportSqliteTests` and `a pulled version's pulled-source row is stored beside its version row, and no other version has one`, the count rising by 3; kit-acceptance MUST pass over OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests with AT-1 and AT-2 expectations and tolerances unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
